6. Concurrency (review LOW). The requested post-write re-read was implemented, then REMOVED as
   unreachable: `gl_accounts_parent_account_id_fkey` references gl_accounts(id), so a concurrent
   child INSERT or reparent UPDATE onto the target needs FOR KEY SHARE on the target row and the
   merge's FOR UPDATE conflicts with it. Proved with two pool clients: both statements return
   55P03 under a 1s lock_timeout while the lock is held, and nothing is written. The first attempt
   at an interleaving test deadlocked (40P01) for exactly this reason, which is what surfaced it.
